==French==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|fr|nrf|caillou}}, from {{der|fr|fro|caillou}}, {{m|fro|kailleu}}, {{m|fro|caillo}}, {{m|fro|caliou}}, {{m|fro|cailloun}}, {{m|fro|calloun}}, related to Judeo-{{cog|fro|chailos}}, {{m|fro|chaillous}} and {{cog|fro|chaille|t=small stone, pebble}}, of {{unc|fr|nocap=1}} origin. Perhaps from a {{der|fr|xtg|*caljo-}} or less likely allied to {{der|fr|odt|kei|t=stone}}, from {{der|fr|gmw-pro|*kagi}}.

Compare {{cog|pcd|cailleu}}, {{cog|wa|caie}}; also {{cog|nl|kei|t=stone, rock}}.

